---
import CapturePageLayout from "@layouts/CapturePageLayout.astro";
import CaptureHero from "@components/capture/CaptureHero.astro";
import CaptureSection from "@components/capture/CaptureSection.astro";
import CaptureTrialCta from "@components/capture/CaptureTrialCta.astro";
import CapturePricing from "@components/capture/CapturePricing.astro";
import Screenshot from "@components/Screenshot.astro";
import StepList from "@components/StepList.astro";
import Step from "@components/Step.astro";
import WithAside from "@components/WithAside.astro";
import practiceClientsImg from "@assets/capture/freeagent/practice-clients.png";
import reviewBillImg from "@assets/capture/freeagent/review-bill.png";
import missingReceiptsTabImg from "@assets/capture/freeagent/missing-receipts-tab.png";
import clientPagePhoneImg from "@assets/capture/freeagent/client-page-phone.png";
import { bulletList, inlineLink, subheading } from "@lib/capture-styles";

const description =
  "Otto reads your clients' receipts and bills, suggests categories from each client's own history, and publishes them to FreeAgent once you've reviewed them.";

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: "With Otto", path: "/" },
  { name: "Otto Capture", path: "/capture/" },
  { name: "FreeAgent", path: "/capture/freeagent/" },
];
---

<CapturePageLayout
  title="Receipt capture for FreeAgent"
  description={description}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  softwareApplication>
  <CaptureHero title="Receipt and bill capture for practices on FreeAgent">
    Otto reads each receipt and bill your clients send, and suggests a category
    for each line from how you've coded that client's bills from the same
    supplier.
    <Fragment slot="after-cta">
      <p>
        You check each document, then publish it to the client's FreeAgent
        company. Nothing reaches FreeAgent until someone in your practice has
        reviewed it and clicked <strong>Publish</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Otto learns one client at a time. His suggestions draw on the bills
        you've published through Capture for that client, including any changes
        you made in review. Bills already in FreeAgent from before you connected
        the client aren't part of that history, so it builds up as you publish.
        He draws on that history only when he's confident the supplier on the
        document is the contact it belongs to. Otherwise, and for a supplier the
        client hasn't used before, he suggests a category from the document
        alone.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </CaptureHero>

  <CaptureSection
    title="Built by a practice, for practices"
    icon="hugeicons:building-03">
    <p>
      We run an accounting practice. We tried a lot of receipt capture tools,
      and none had the mix of features and pricing that worked for our clients.
      The small rough edges added up too, using them day in, day out.
    </p>
    <p>
      So we built Otto Capture around the jobs that took our time, and those
      jobs are the same whichever accounting platform a client is on. Clients
      send documents without creating an account. They answer their missing
      receipts from one list, not a spreadsheet. And Otto reads every line and
      suggests a category from that client's own history.
    </p>
  </CaptureSection>

  <CaptureSection
    title="Connecting your FreeAgent practice"
    tone="soft"
    icon="hugeicons:plug-socket">
    <p>
      Connect Capture to your Practice Dashboard once, then add clients from it.
      Capture lists the clients your practice manages, each with its entity
      type, and you tick the ones to add. Each becomes a client in Capture with
      its own inbox and settings, and every one shares the practice connection.
    </p>
    <p>
      To add more later, go back to the same list. Clients you've already added
      show as <strong>Connected</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can also connect a single FreeAgent company on its own, signed in as a
      user who can manage bills in it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Capture then brings across what Otto needs to code and publish: contacts,
      categories, tax rates, currencies, and the company's details. If you add a
      category in FreeAgent later, refresh the client's data in Capture to bring
      it across.
    </p>
    <Screenshot
      src={practiceClientsImg}
      alt="The Add FreeAgent clients page, listing the practice's FreeAgent clients by entity type, with two ticked and one already connected"
    />
    <p>
      Permissions, and everything Capture brings across, are covered in{" "}
      <a
        href="https://support.withotto.app/capture/platforms/freeagent/"
        class={inlineLink}>
        Otto Capture's FreeAgent guide
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </CaptureSection>

  <CaptureSection
    title="From a client's document to FreeAgent"
    icon="hugeicons:route-01">
    <StepList>
      <Step>
        Your client sends a receipt or bill by email, through their submission
        page, or on WhatsApp.
      </Step>
      <Step>
        Otto reads it, line by line, matches the supplier to one of the client's
        FreeAgent contacts, and suggests a category and tax rate for each line.
      </Step>
      <Step>
        Someone in your practice checks it and changes anything that needs it.
      </Step>
      <Step>
        You click <strong>Publish</strong>, and Otto publishes it to the
        client's FreeAgent company.
      </Step>
    </StepList>
    <Screenshot
      src={reviewBillImg}
      alt="A bill in review, each line with a category and tax rate, ready to publish to FreeAgent"
    />
    <p>
      Otto publishes bills, bill credit notes, sales invoices, and credit notes
      to FreeAgent.
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-4 pt-8">
      <h3 class={subheading}>Line items and categories</h3>
      <p>
        Each line item you've reviewed becomes a line on the bill or invoice in
        FreeAgent, with its category and tax rate.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-4 pt-8">
      <h3 class={subheading}>How each document arrives</h3>
      <p>
        Bills and bill credit notes go straight into the client's FreeAgent
        company, with the original document attached. Sales invoices and credit
        notes arrive as drafts.
      </p>
      <p>
        Otto attaches the original document up to 5 MB. Where FreeAgent doesn't
        accept the file type, such as an iPhone photo saved as HEIC or a Word
        file, Capture attaches a PDF or image version of it. FreeAgent doesn't
        let Capture attach files to sales invoices or credit notes, so they
        publish without one, and the original stays in Capture.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-4 pt-8">
      <h3 class={subheading}>Contacts</h3>
      <p>
        Otto matches the supplier or customer on each document to the client's
        FreeAgent contacts. He remembers which contact you published each
        supplier name against, for that client. Where a name doesn't match a
        FreeAgent contact exactly, he uses that to match the next document. If
        the contact isn't in FreeAgent yet, you can create it during review, and
        Capture adds it to FreeAgent when you publish.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-4 pt-8">
      <h3 class={subheading}>Foreign currency</h3>
      <p>
        A document in any currency FreeAgent supports publishes in that
        currency, and FreeAgent applies its own exchange rate.
      </p>
      <p>
        For a currency FreeAgent doesn't support, convert the document during
        review. You can also convert a document FreeAgent would accept, for
        example so the bill matches the amount that cleared the bank. Enter the
        total the client was actually charged, and Otto restates every line at
        that rate. He puts anything left over from rounding on the most suitable
        line, so the lines add up to your total exactly. He also compares your
        total with the market rate on the document's date. Where the two differ
        by more than he'd expect, he asks you to check the total before applying
        it, which catches a mistyped figure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </CaptureSection>

  <CaptureSection
    title="Chasing missing receipts"
    tone="soft"
    width="wide"
    icon="hugeicons:file-search">
    <WithAside steps={5} listAsideFrom={2}>
      <p>
        Capture turns the payments you have no paperwork for into a list the
        client answers.
      </p>
      <StepList slot="list">
        <Step>
          On the client's <strong>Missing receipts</strong> tab, choose the
          dates and click <strong>Fetch transactions</strong>. Capture reads the
          unexplained bank transactions from every bank account in the client's
          FreeAgent company that isn't hidden, credit cards included. The dates
          start at the last six months, and you can change either one.
          <Screenshot
            slot="media"
            src={missingReceiptsTabImg}
            alt="A FreeAgent client's Missing receipts tab, with the dates to fetch, the transactions stored, and how many on the client's list are still unanswered"
          />
        </Step>
        <Step>
          Exclude the payments the client doesn't need to explain, such as
          transfers between their own accounts, and any that shouldn't be seen
          by everyone with the link, such as salaries. Every other payment goes
          on the list.
        </Step>
        <Step>
          Share the client's link, when and how it suits your practice and the
          client. Capture doesn't contact the client, so it fits the way you
          already work with them.
        </Step>
        <Step>
          Your client opens the link on any device, with no login, and answers
          each payment with a receipt, a short note, or both.
        </Step>
        <Step>
          Receipts go into that client's review queue like any other document,
          with the note alongside when you review it. You can see which payments
          are still waiting for an answer.
        </Step>
      </StepList>
      <Screenshot
        slot="list-aside"
        src={clientPagePhoneImg}
        alt="A client's list of payments on a phone, each with a button to send a receipt and a button to add a note"
        class="mx-auto max-w-[280px]"
      />
      <div slot="after" class="space-y-4">
        <p>
          Fetch again whenever you want the list up to date. A payment explained
          in FreeAgent since the last fetch comes off the client's list when you
          next update it. Anything you've excluded stays excluded, and anything
          the client has answered keeps its answer.
        </p>
        <p>
          The link can go to whoever can find the receipts, such as the people
          at the client who hold the company cards. Your contact at the client
          can pass it on, or you can send it to each person yourself. Anyone
          with the link can see the date, description, amount, and bank account
          of each payment on the list, and your admins can replace the link or
          switch the page off at any time.
        </p>
        <p>
          Capture reads the transactions only when you click{" "}
          <strong>Fetch transactions</strong>, and changes nothing in FreeAgent.
          Fetching transactions and preparing lists cost nothing extra. The full
          steps are in the{" "}
          <a
            href="https://support.withotto.app/capture/missing-receipts/freeagent/"
            class={inlineLink}>
            guide to missing receipts for FreeAgent clients
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </div>
    </WithAside>
  </CaptureSection>

  <CaptureSection
    title="How clients send documents"
    icon="hugeicons:inbox-upload">
    <p>
      Each client has its own email address, submission page, and WhatsApp
      invite link. You choose which of them to give the client, so they use the
      routes that suit them and your practice.
    </p>
    <ul class={bulletList}>
      <li>
        <strong>Email:</strong> the client forwards or sends documents to their
        own address.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Submission page:</strong> they upload files from any device.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>WhatsApp:</strong> they send a photo or file after joining
        through the invite link.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Whoever holds the receipts uses the route that suits them. They don't
      create an account or install anything, and you don't register them in
      advance. You can also upload files yourself. Everything arrives in the
      same review queue, whichever way it's sent. There's more on each route on{" "}
      <a href="/capture/" class={inlineLink}>
        the Otto Capture page
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </CaptureSection>

  <CaptureSection
    title="What it costs"
    tone="soft"
    width="default"
    icon="hugeicons:coins-01">
    <p class="max-w-3xl">
      Otto Capture is priced per client, per month, on three tiers, and each
      client sits on whichever tier costs least for what it published that
      month.
    </p>
    <CapturePricing variant="compact" />
    <p class="max-w-3xl pt-4">
      Prices exclude VAT. Full pricing is on{" "}
      <a href="/capture/" class={inlineLink}>
        the Otto Capture page
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </CaptureSection>

  <CaptureTrialCta
    title="Try it on as many FreeAgent clients as you like"
    secondaryHref="https://www.freeagent.com/integrations/withotto/"
    secondaryLabel="Find Otto Capture in FreeAgent's integrations">
    <p>
      The free 30-day trial has no limit on clients or documents, so connect
      your Practice Dashboard and add as many clients as you like. We'd suggest
      putting Otto through his paces: include the clients whose paperwork takes
      longest each month, and send in a few weeks of their receipts and bills.
      Review them with every line already read and a category suggested, then
      fetch their unexplained transactions and send them their missing receipts
      link.
    </p>
    <p>Otto Capture is available to UK accounting and bookkeeping practices.</p>
    <Fragment slot="note">
      Your clients can be on any mix of Xero, FreeAgent, and QuickBooks Online.
      On QuickBooks Online, Otto publishes purchases.
    </Fragment>
  </CaptureTrialCta>
</CapturePageLayout>
